{"id":"st2036-3","designation":"ST 2036-3","title":"Ultra High Definition Television — Mapping into Single-link or Multi-link 10 Gb/s Serial Signal/Data Interface","state":"active","suite":"2036","official":{"family_url":"https://pub.smpte.org/doc/st2036-3/","latest_url":"https://pub.smpte.org/latest/st2036-3/","checked_at":"2026-11-11"},"scope":"This document defines UHDTV and HDR UHDTV video payload mapping into Single-link, Dual-link, Quad-link or Octa-link 10G-SDI Mode D defined in SMPTE ST 435-2. This document also defines mapping of ANC, Audio Data, payload ID and other ancillary data formatted as defined in SMPTE ST 291-1. The “Basic Stream” complies with the interleaved data stream defined in SMPTE ST 292-1 and is utilized as the input source stream for the 10G-SDI. When transporting UHDTV1,2 signals through a single single-mode fiber, WDM (Wavelength Division Multiplexing) or DWDM (Dense Wavelength Division Multiplexing) as defined in Section 6.4 and Section 7.4 can be used.","outline":[{"level":1,"title":"1 Scope","page":3},{"level":1,"title":"2 Conformance Notation","page":3},{"level":1,"title":"3 Normative References","page":3},{"level":1,"title":"4 Definition of Terms","page":4},{"level":1,"title":"5 System Overview","page":5},{"level":1,"title":"6 UHDTV1 Mapping into Single-link or Dual-link 10G-SDI","page":6},{"level":2,"title":"6.1 Video Payload Mapping","page":6},{"level":2,"title":"6.2 Single-link 10G-SDI for System U1.1 to U1.5","page":8},{"level":2,"title":"6.3 Dual-link 10G-SDI for System U1.6 to U1.9","page":8},{"level":2,"title":"6.4 Optical Interface Characteristics","page":10},{"level":2,"title":"6.5 ANC/Audio Data Mapping","page":10},{"level":3,"title":"6.5.1 ANC Data Mapping","page":10},{"level":3,"title":"6.5.2 Audio Data Mapping","page":10},{"level":3,"title":"6.5.3 Payload ID Mapping","page":11},{"level":2,"title":"6.6 Blanking Data (Informative)","page":13},{"level":1,"title":"7 UHDTV2 Mapping into Quad-link or Octa-link 10G-SDI","page